(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test12_1B"] = [{"id":"56ec23a0","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Hiroshi Senju is known worldwide for his paintings of waterfalls. These paintings are large and tend not to show the entire waterfall. Instead, Senju focuses on just the point where the falling water reaches the pool below, keeping the top of the waterfall out of view. While Senju’s paintings are rooted in art movements originating in the United States, the artist uses traditional Japanese techniques and materials that make his work instantly recognizable.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Hiroshi Senju is known worldwide for his paintings of waterfalls. These paintings are large and tend not to show the entire waterfall. Instead,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Senju focuses on just the point where the falling water reaches the pool below, keeping the top of the waterfall out of view. While Senju’s","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"paintings are rooted in art movements originating in the United States, the artist uses traditional Japanese techniques and materials that make","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"his work instantly recognizable.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It introduces an artist and then explains some common characteristics of well-known paintings by that artist.","It explains a specific painting technique and then provides examples of artists who use the technique.","It describes a famous painting and then compares it to a lesser-known painting from the same time period.","It gives an opinion on an artist and then suggests multiple reasons why the artist’s work has been largely overlooked."]},{"id":"2903a041","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Using NASA’s powerful James Webb Space Telescope (JWST), Mercedes L ópez-Morales and colleagues measured the wavelengths of light traveling through the atmosphere of WASP-39b, an exoplanet, or planet outside our solar system. Different molecules absorb different wavelengths of light, and the wavelength measurements showed the presence of carbon dioxide (CO₂) in WASP-39b’s atmosphere. This finding not only offers the first decisive evidence of CO₂ in the atmosphere of an exoplanet but also illustrates the potential for future scientific breakthroughs held by the JWST.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Using NASA’s powerful James Webb Space Telescope (JWST), Mercedes López-Morales and colleagues measured the wavelengths of light","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"traveling through the atmosphere of WASP-39b, an exoplanet, or planet outside our solar system. Different molecules absorb different","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"wavelengths of light, and the wavelength measurements showed the presence of carbon dioxide (CO₂) in WASP-39b’s atmosphere. This finding","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"not only offers the first decisive evidence of CO₂ in the atmosphere of an exoplanet but also illustrates the potential for future scientific","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"breakthroughs held by the JWST.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It discusses a method used by some researchers, then states why an alternative method is superior to it.","It describes how researchers made a scientific discovery, then explains the importance of that discovery.","It outlines the steps taken in a scientific study, then presents a hypothesis based on that study.","It examines how a group of scientists reached a conclusion, then shows how other scientists have challenged that conclusion."]},{"id":"0afb2ac4","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Ancient Inca inhabiting the Andes Mountains used terraces, rows of flattened land with built-in irrigation systems, to grow crops at different altitudes. This method of farming proved to be highly ______, as evidenced by the great number and variety of crops grown at that time.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Ancient Inca inhabiting the Andes Mountains used terraces, rows of flattened land with built-in irrigation systems, to grow crops at different","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"altitudes. This method of farming proved to be highly ______, as evidenced by the great number and variety of crops grown at that time.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["chaotic","uniform","effective","burdensome"]},{"id":"d9915c15","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In 2020, rap artist and professor A.D. Carson published the first peer-reviewed rap album about his experiences with Black masculinity called “i used to love to dream.” Typically in peer review, experts evaluate scholarly articles prior to publication. For Carson’s album, dubbed a “mixtap/e/ssay,” peer review involved both scholars and rap artists. In combining elements of a mixtape album with scholarly essays that connect Carson’s lyrics to historical and contemporary contexts for listeners both inside and outside academia, Carson’s album helped redefine how scholarship is created and shared.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2020, rap artist and professor A.D. Carson published the first peer-reviewed rap album about his experiences with Black masculinity called “i","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"used to love to dream.” Typically in peer review, experts evaluate scholarly articles prior to publication. For Carson’s album, dubbed a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"“mixtap/e/ssay,” peer review involved both scholars and rap artists. In combining elements of a mixtape album with scholarly essays that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"connect Carson’s lyrics to historical and contemporary contexts for listeners both inside and outside academia, Carson’s album helped redefine","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"how scholarship is created and shared.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To compare the relative public impact of scholarly articles and albums","To capture one scholar’s opinion of a new rap album","To explain why a certain rap album is particularly innovative","To describe how each step of the peer review process unfolds"]},{"id":"bdab32fc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Cucurbits, a group of plants that includes squash and melons, relied on mastodons to spread their seeds in the Ice Age. When these animals died out, cucurbits faced extinction in turn, having lost their means of seed dispersal. Around this time, however, the ancestors of Indigenous peoples in North America began raising cucurbits as crops, thus ______ the plants’ survival.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Cucurbits, a group of plants that includes squash and melons, relied on mastodons to spread their seeds in the Ice Age. When these animals","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"died out, cucurbits faced extinction in turn, having lost their means of seed dispersal. Around this time, however, the ancestors of Indigenous","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"peoples in North America began raising cucurbits as crops, thus ______ the plants’ survival.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["verifying","multiplying","comforting","ensuring"]},{"id":"4b4ab04e","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 Mycoprotein is a fungal biomass that can be eaten as an alternative to meat. Studies of the environmental impact of its manufacture generally agree it is lower than that of beef and closer to that of chicken or pork. But the expense of producing mycoprotein restricts its availability to a few countries with postindustrial economies. Knowing that cost reductions would expand access to mycoprotein, biochemists are exploring solutions, such as a cheaper substrate to feed the mycoprotein as it grows. Text 2 Cattle farming is a principal cause of global deforestation, and a study by Florian Humpen öder and his colleagues found that replacing 20% of beef consumption worldwide with consumption of mycoprotein would cut deforestation by half if accomplished over the next thirty years. However, this would likely involve only a small change in agricultural water consumption, since water once dedicated to raising cattle would be diverted to raising crops instead.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Mycoprotein is a fungal biomass that can be eaten as an alternative to meat. Studies of the environmental impact of its manufacture generally","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"agree it is lower than that of beef and closer to that of chicken or pork. But the expense of producing mycoprotein restricts its availability to a few","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"countries with postindustrial economies. Knowing that cost reductions would expand access to mycoprotein, biochemists are exploring","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"solutions, such as a cheaper substrate to feed the mycoprotein as it grows.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Cattle farming is a principal cause of global deforestation, and a study by Florian Humpenöder and his colleagues found that replacing 20% of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"beef consumption worldwide with consumption of mycoprotein would cut deforestation by half if accomplished over the next thirty years.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"However, this would likely involve only a small change in agricultural water consumption, since water once dedicated to raising cattle would be","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"diverted to raising crops instead.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 1 most likely respond to the study findings mentioned in Text 2?","choices":["By emphasizing that since agricultural water consumption would remain static in the event of replacing beef consumption with mycoprotein consumption, an effort must be made to substitute mycoprotein for chicken and pork in diets as well","By asserting that the development of a more inexpensive substrate for mycoprotein production would contribute to the goal of decreasing worldwide deforestation over time","By noting that most people would be more likely to use mycoprotein as a substitute for chicken or pork in their diets than as a substitute for beef","By pointing out that some countries are responsible for greater deforestation than others and thus, to have any significant effect on the environment, will have to replace more than 20% of their beef consumption with mycoprotein"]},{"id":"06b96bfc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"A musician and member of the Quechua of Peru, Renata Flores Rivera was eager to promote the Quechua language in her music, but she was ______ speaking it. She met this challenge by asking her grandmother, a native speaker of Quechua, to help her pronounce words in her song lyrics and also by taking classes in the language.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"A musician and member of the Quechua of Peru, Renata Flores Rivera was eager to promote the Quechua language in her music, but she was","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"______ speaking it. She met this challenge by asking her grandmother, a native speaker of Quechua, to help her pronounce words in her song","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"lyrics and also by taking classes in the language.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["prepared for","inexperienced with","skilled in","excited about"]},{"id":"0ed8f24f","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"K.D. Leka and colleagues found that the Sun’s corona provides an advance indication of solar flares —intense eruptions of electromagnetic radiation that emanate from active regions in the Sun’s photosphere and can interfere with telecommunications on Earth. Preceding a flare, the corona temporarily exhibits increased brightness above the region where the flare is ______.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"K.D. Leka and colleagues found that the Sun’s corona provides an advance indication of solar flares—intense eruptions of electromagnetic","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"radiation that emanate from active regions in the Sun’s photosphere and can interfere with telecommunications on Earth. Preceding a flare, the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"corona temporarily exhibits increased brightness above the region where the flare is ______.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["antecedent","impending","innocuous","perpetual"]},{"id":"23ecf625","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Conservationists worldwide are working to protect ecosystems from habitat destruction and biodiversity loss, and in many cases, initiatives that rely on natural features or processes can help address such challenges. In response to a rapidly dwindling population of blueback salmon, the Quinault Indian Nation (a tribe in Washington State) partnered with the conservation organization Wild Salmon Center to restore naturally occurring logjams in the Quinault River. The logjams create shady pools where the blueback salmon can rest and spawn, thus promoting blueback population recovery.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Conservationists worldwide are working to protect ecosystems from habitat destruction and biodiversity loss, and in many cases, initiatives that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rely on natural features or processes can help address such challenges. In response to a rapidly dwindling population of blueback salmon, the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Quinault Indian Nation (a tribe in Washington State) partnered with the conservation organization Wild Salmon Center to restore naturally","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"occurring logjams in the Quinault River. The logjams create shady pools where the blueback salmon can rest and spawn, thus promoting","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"blueback population recovery.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["A partnership between the Quinault Indian Nation and Wild Salmon Center shows the importance of collaborative approaches to preserving biodiversity.","Nature-based approaches can be effective ways to achieve conservation goals.","As indicated by a recent project, logjams help the blueback salmon thrive and reproduce.","Scientists now realize that nature-based conservation methods offer better long-term solutions to environmental issues than methods that are not nature-based do."]},{"id":"2584bcfb","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Matthew D. Rocklage and team examined whether consumer ratings of movies can predict box office success. The team considered both numeric star ratings and written reviews in their research. To analyze the written reviews, the team measured the emotionality — the degree to which a written review expresses an emotional reaction — of user reviews on a movie rating website, assigning each review an emotionality score. After reviewing this research, a student argues that the emotionality of movie reviews is unrelated to a movie’s success at the box office. Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Matthew D. Rocklage and team examined whether consumer ratings of movies can predict box office success. The team considered both","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"numeric star ratings and written reviews in their research. To analyze the written reviews, the team measured the emotionality—the degree to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"which a written review expresses an emotional reaction—of user reviews on a movie rating website, assigning each review an emotionality score.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"After reviewing this research, a student argues that the emotionality of movie reviews is unrelated to a movie’s success at the box office.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken the student’s conclusion?","choices":["Movies that had the highest average emotionality scores received the lowest average star ratings on the movie rating website.","The average emotionality score of a movie’s reviews was a positive predictor of that movie’s box office earnings.","More than half of the movies that the team examined received an average star rating of 3 out of 5 stars.","The movies that were most successful at the box office tended to have high average star ratings."]},{"id":"df8caadd","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Partial List of Candidate Species for De-extinction Common name Scientific name Became extinct Huia Heteralocha acutirostris 1907 Caribbean monk seal Monachus tropicalis 1952 Passenger pigeon Ectopistes migratorius 1914 Saber-toothed cat Smilodon 11,000 years before present Woolly mammoth Mammuthus primigenius 6,400 years before present The passage of time is among the many obstacles faced by scientists who are pursuing de-extinction efforts — that is, efforts to use breeding or a mixture of cloning and genetic engineering to bring back extinct species. Specifically, researchers are concerned that the longer a species has been extinct, the less likely it is that a suitable habitat still exists for that species. Among candidate species for de-extinction, this problem would be especially concerning for the ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"table","title":"Partial List of Candidate Species for De-extinction","headers":["Common name","Scientific name","Became extinct"],"rows":[["Huia","Heteralocha acutirostris","1907"],["Caribbean monk seal","Monachus tropicalis","1952"],["Passenger pigeon","Ectopistes migratorius","1914"],["Saber-toothed cat","Smilodon","11,000 years before present"],["Woolly mammoth","Mammuthus primigenius","6,400 years before present"]]},{"type":"text","text":"The passage of time is among the many obstacles faced by scientists who are pursuing de-extinction efforts — that is, efforts to use breeding or a mixture of cloning and genetic engineering to bring back extinct species. Specifically, researchers are concerned that the longer a species has been extinct, the less likely it is that a suitable habitat still exists for that species. Among candidate species for de-extinction, this problem would be especially concerning for the ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?","choices":["passenger pigeon (Ectopistes migratorius), which became extinct only a few years after the huia (Heteralocha acutirostris).","saber-toothed cat (Smilodon), which became extinct 11,000 years ago.","woolly mammoth (Mammuthus primigenius), which became extinct several thousand years before the saber-toothed cat (Smilodon).","Caribbean monk seal (Monachus tropicalis), which became extinct in 1952."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Partial List","List of Candidate Species for","for De-extinction"]},{"id":"d95a0bb8","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"The ratio of methane to other atmospheric constituents — represented by a measure called the methane mole fraction —influences a variety of meteorological phenomena, notably precipitation and humidity. For Titan, Saturn’s largest moon, the observational data that exist are too sparse and discrepant to fully constrain the range of the methane mole fraction at various atmospheric levels. Juan Lora and colleagues point out that outputs of the IPSL atmospheric model of Titan, which track closely to observations in some respects, reflect how the model’s developers’ responded to this challenge: by prescribing a uniform methane mole fraction for the lowest level of the atmosphere. It is therefore important to note that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The ratio of methane to other atmospheric constituents—represented by a measure called the methane mole fraction—influences a variety of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"meteorological phenomena, notably precipitation and humidity. For Titan, Saturn’s largest moon, the observational data that exist are too sparse","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and discrepant to fully constrain the range of the methane mole fraction at various atmospheric levels. Juan Lora and colleagues point out that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"outputs of the IPSL atmospheric model of Titan, which track closely to observations in some respects, reflect how the model’s developers","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"responded to this challenge: by prescribing a uniform methane mole fraction for the lowest level of the atmosphere. It is therefore important to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"note that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["some disagreements between the model’s simulations of Titan’s precipitation and humidity and the moon’s actual precipitation and humidity are to be expected.","further observations of Titan may clarify the moon’s methane mole fraction sufficiently for the model to employ a single value rather than a range.","even though the model’s outputs sometimes agree with observational data, Titan’s real methane mole fraction is likely higher than the methane mole fraction used in the model.","inconsistencies across the model’s simulations of Titan’s precipitation and humidity could be attributable to variations in the moon’s methane mole fraction."]},{"id":"b470d853","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Recreation Visits by Month to Four US National Parks during the Peak Season in 2021 1,100 1,000 Number of recreation visits 900 (in thousands of visitors) 800 700 600 500 400 300 200 100 0 ly t ne Ju us Ju g Au Month Yellowstone Zion Grand Canyon Rocky Mountain In 2021, four of the United States national parks that were among the most visited were Grand Canyon National Park, Rocky Mountain National Park, Yellowstone National Park, and Zion National Park. The graph shows the number of visits for recreation to each of these parks during the three-month period with the highest number of visitors. A student notes that among the parks shown in the graph, the park with the highest monthly recreation visits in all three months was ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Recreation Visits by Month to Four US National Parks during the Peak Season in 2021 — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"In 2021, four of the United States national parks that were among the most visited were Grand Canyon National Park, Rocky Mountain National Park, Yellowstone National Park, and Zion National Park. The graph shows the number of visits for recreation to each of these parks during the three-month period with the highest number of visitors. A student notes that among the parks shown in the graph, the park with the highest monthly recreation visits in all three months was ______"}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the text?","choices":["Zion National Park.","Rocky Mountain National Park.","Yellowstone National Park.","Grand Canyon National Park."],"unusable":"missing graph"},{"id":"f39507a3","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"One challenge when researching whether holding elected office changes a person’s behavior is the problem of ensuring that the experiment has an appropriate control group. To reveal the effect of holding office, researchers must compare people who hold elected office with people who do not hold office but who are otherwise similar to the office-holders. Since researchers are unable to control which politicians win elections, they therefore ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"One challenge when researching whether holding elected office changes a person’s behavior is the problem of ensuring that the experiment has","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"an appropriate control group. To reveal the effect of holding office, researchers must compare people who hold elected office with people who","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"do not hold office but who are otherwise similar to the office-holders. Since researchers are unable to control which politicians win elections,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"they therefore ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["struggle to find valid data about the behavior of politicians who do not currently hold office.","can only conduct valid studies with people who have previously held office rather than people who presently hold office.","should select a control group of people who differ from office-holders in several significant ways.","will find it difficult to identify a group of people who can function as an appropriate control group for their studies."]},{"id":"df37c087","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Weight of Three Aerial Robots 550 500 450 400 Weight (grams) 350 300 250 200 150 100 50 0 Robot Ultra-Fast Robot Hand Permanent Magnet Hand Yale Model T Aerial robots vary considerably in their holding force; the Ultra-Fast Robot Hand, for example, has a holding force of 56 newtons, more than twice that of the Permanent Magnet Hand and more than four times that of the Yale Model T. Since an aerial robot must lift its own weight along with its cargo, engineer Jiawei Meng and colleagues used a ratio of each robot’s holding force to the robot’s weight to calculate payload capacity, with higher ratios corresponding to greater capacity, concluding that the Ultra-Fast Robot Hand has a higher payload capacity than the Yale Model T.","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Weight of Three Aerial Robots — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"Aerial robots vary considerably in their holding force; the Ultra-Fast Robot Hand, for example, has a holding force of 56 newtons, more than twice that of the Permanent Magnet Hand and more than four times that of the Yale Model T. Since an aerial robot must lift its own weight along with its cargo, engineer Jiawei Meng and colleagues used a ratio of each robot’s holding force to the robot’s weight to calculate payload capacity, with higher ratios corresponding to greater capacity, concluding that the Ultra-Fast Robot Hand has a higher payload capacity than the Yale Model T."}],"question":"Which choice best describes data in the graph that support Meng and colleagues’ conclusion?","choices":["The Ultra-Fast Robot Hand and the Yale Model T each weigh more than 450 grams.","The Ultra-Fast Robot Hand and the Yale Model T each weigh more than the Permanent Magnet Hand does.","The Yale Model T has a lower holding force than the Permanent Magnet Hand despite weighing more.","The Ultra-Fast Robot Hand weighs only slightly more than the Yale Model T does."]},{"id":"e060dd6b","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Recordings of electrical activity in the brain, ______ increased activity in brain areas associated with suppressing motor functions.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Recordings of electrical activity in the brain, ______ increased activity in brain areas associated with suppressing motor functions.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["electrograms show that while responding to hypothetical match scenarios, the most highly skilled soccer players have","the most highly skilled soccer players responding to hypothetical match scenarios have electrograms that show","responses to hypothetical match scenarios show that the most highly skilled soccer players have electrograms with","hypothetical match scenario responses show that the most highly skilled soccer players captured in electrograms have"]},{"id":"8b002b08","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Many Samoans enjoy a sport called kilikiti. This bat-and-ball game was derived from ______ kilikiti differs from cricket in a few key ways.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Many Samoans enjoy a sport called kilikiti. This bat-and-ball game was derived from ______ kilikiti differs from cricket in a few key ways.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["cricket but:","cricket but,","cricket, but","cricket, but,"]},{"id":"e38b3e4f","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"The radiation that ______ during the decay of radioactive atomic nuclei is known as gamma radiation.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The radiation that ______ during the decay of radioactive atomic nuclei is known as gamma radiation.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["occurs","have occurred","occur","are occurring"]},{"id":"1684b237","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"One of the few African American global explorers during the turn of the 20th century, ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"One of the few African American global explorers during the turn of the 20th century, ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Matthew Henson made several treks across Greenland between 1891 and 1909.","1891 and 1909 were the years between which Matthew Henson made several treks across Greenland.","Greenland was where Matthew Henson made several treks between 1891 and 1909.","several treks across Greenland were made by Matthew Henson between 1891 and 1909."]},{"id":"ce81d0b7","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"The life spans of rockfish vary greatly by species. For instance, the colorful calico rockfish (Sebastes dallii) can survive for a little over a ______ the rougheye rockfish (Sebastes aleutianus) boasts a maximum life span of about two centuries.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The life spans of rockfish vary greatly by species. For instance, the colorful calico rockfish (Sebastes dallii) can survive for a little over a ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the rougheye rockfish (Sebastes aleutianus) boasts a maximum life span of about two centuries.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["decade: while","decade. While","decade; while","decade, while"]},{"id":"cf08e2fd","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"From 1912 to 1951, Charlotta Bass owned and operated the newspaper The California Eagle. While it was under Bass’s leadership, The Eagle ______ one of the US’s most influential Black-owned newspapers.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"From 1912 to 1951, Charlotta Bass owned and operated the newspaper The California Eagle. While it was under Bass’s leadership, The Eagle","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"______ one of the US’s most influential Black-owned newspapers.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["will become","became","is becoming","to become"]},{"id":"5a5e22b5","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Gravitational waves are powerful ripples that originate in deep space and eventually pass through Earth. The Laser Interferometer Gravitational Wave Observatory (LIGO) is a physics study that began in 2002. LIGO’s goal is to detect and analyze gravitational waves. LIGO uses a pair of massive gravitational wave detectors called interferometers that are thousands of miles apart. In 2015, for the first time in history, LIGO researchers detected a gravitational wave passing through Earth. The student wants to present LIGO’s aim and methodology.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Gravitational waves are powerful ripples that originate in deep space and eventually pass through Earth.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The Laser Interferometer Gravitational Wave Observatory (LIGO) is a physics study that began in 2002.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"LIGO’s goal is to detect and analyze gravitational waves.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"LIGO uses a pair of massive gravitational wave detectors called interferometers that are thousands of miles apart.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"In 2015, for the first time in history, LIGO researchers detected a gravitational wave passing through Earth.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["In 2015, LIGO’s massive interferometers detected a powerful ripple that originated in deep space and eventually passed through Earth.","Though the physics study LIGO began in 2002, its massive interferometers didn’t detect a gravitational wave until 2015.","To achieve its aims, LIGO uses a pair of massive interferometers that are thousands of miles apart.","A physics study designed to detect and analyze gravitational waves, LIGO uses a pair of massive interferometers that are thousands of miles apart."]},{"id":"3fd0ab63","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Voting members of the 2002 Latin Grammys were impressed by Banda Cuisillos’s album Puras Rancheras Con Cuisillos and its contribution to the banda genre, a form of regional Mexican music featuring large ensembles of wind instruments and drums that first developed in southern and central Mexico in the mid-nineteenth century. ______ they awarded the group the Best Banda Album award.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Voting members of the 2002 Latin Grammys were impressed by Banda Cuisillos’s album Puras Rancheras Con Cuisillos and its contribution to the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"banda genre, a form of regional Mexican music featuring large ensembles of wind instruments and drums that first developed in southern and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"central Mexico in the mid-nineteenth century. ______ they awarded the group the Best Banda Album award.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In contrast,","Meanwhile,","Nevertheless,","Accordingly,"]},{"id":"42d92dea","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Before it unveiled a massive new gallery in 2009, the Art Institute of Chicago was only able to display about 5% of its art collection. ______ the museum is able to display close to 30% of its collection.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Before it unveiled a massive new gallery in 2009, the Art Institute of Chicago was only able to display about 5% of its art collection. ______ the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"museum is able to display close to 30% of its collection.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Additionally,","For example,","Nevertheless,","Today,"]},{"id":"49ecf985","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"On March 3, 1991, Switzerland’s government lowered the minimum voting age for its citizens from 20 to 18 years old. ______ many people in Switzerland gained a new opportunity to participate in their country’s political process.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"On March 3, 1991, Switzerland’s government lowered the minimum voting age for its citizens from 20 to 18 years old. ______ many people in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Switzerland gained a new opportunity to participate in their country’s political process.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Nevertheless,","As a result,","By contrast,","Similarly,"]},{"id":"48d0bb34","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Sam Maloof (1916 – 2009) was an American woodworker and furniture designer. He was the son of Lebanese immigrants. He received a genius grant from the John D. and Catherine T. MacArthur Foundation in 1985. The Museum of Fine Arts in Boston, Massachusetts, owns a rocking chair that Maloof made from walnut wood. The armrests and the seat of the chair are sleek and contoured, and the back consists of seven spindle-like slats. The student wants to describe the rocking chair to an audience unfamiliar with Sam Maloof.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Sam Maloof (1916–2009) was an American woodworker and furniture designer.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"He was the son of Lebanese immigrants.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"He received a “genius grant” from the John D. and Catherine T. MacArthur Foundation in 1985.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The Museum of Fine Arts in Boston, Massachusetts, owns a rocking chair that Maloof made from walnut wood.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The armrests and the seat of the chair are sleek and contoured, and the back consists of seven spindle-like slats.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["With its sleek, contoured armrests and seat, the walnut rocking chair in Boston’s Museum of Fine Arts is just one piece of furniture created by American woodworker Sam Maloof.","Sam Maloof was born in 1916 and died in 2009, and during his life, he made a chair that you can see if you visit the Museum of Fine Arts in Boston.","Furniture designer Sam Maloof was a recipient of one of the John D. and Catherine T. MacArthur Foundation’s “genius grants.”","The rocking chair is made from walnut, and it has been shaped such that its armrests and seat are sleek and contoured."]},{"id":"6036ad0e","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In 2014, Nestor Gomez won his first-ever storytelling competition, relating a tale about his life as a Guatemalan immigrant living in Chicago. ______ in 2017, Gomez created the show 80 Minutes Around the World as a platform for others to share stories about their immigration experiences.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2014, Nestor Gomez won his first-ever storytelling competition, relating a tale about his life as a Guatemalan immigrant living in Chicago.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"______ in 2017, Gomez created the show 80 Minutes Around the World as a platform for others to share stories about their immigration","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"experiences.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Instead,","For example,","Later,","In other words,"]}];
